    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0786" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8262</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-26T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 26, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 23, 1 p.m. For your information and guidance. The President, and
                    State, War and Treasury Departments all favor financial assistance to China for
                    military expedition. The matter awaits approval of the Allied Council. What is
                    foundation of your statement that Allies have agreed to the policy?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
